6. INTELLIGENT MODEL ROUTING
==================================================

Implement an intelligent model router.

The router should analyze each task and select a suitable configured model.

Examples:

- Simple conversations → Fast language model.
- Complex reasoning → Reasoning model.
- Programming → Coding-capable model.
- Image understanding → Vision model.
- Image generation → Image generation model.
- Speech recognition → Speech-to-text model.
- Audio generation → Text-to-speech or audio model.
- Research → Model with suitable search and reasoning tools.
- Long documents → Model with sufficient context capacity.

Routing considerations:

- Task complexity.
- Model capability.
- Latency.
- Cost.
- Token limits.
- Provider availability.
- User preference.
- Privacy requirements.
- Local versus cloud execution.

Allow manual model override.

Implement fallback routing only when an alternative model genuinely supports the required task.

Never silently send private user data to another provider without appropriate disclosure and permission.

